0s"Taphrinales (Taphrina)." 1a : Frb absent ; parasitic, forming ± conspicuous galls on leaves and fruits of living trees and shrubs. Asci formed in a palisade within the host epidermis. 011170 Taphrinales (Taphrina). 0
0 1b : Frb present or if not asci intermixed with paraphyses ; saprotrophic, parasitic or mycorrhizal.0112802
0 2a : Frb an apothecium or a hypogeous, tuber-like cleistothecium.0223903
0 2b : Frb a perithecium or a tiny, epigeous cleistothecium.02241008
0s"Eurotiales (Elaphomyces)." 3a : Frb hypogeous, hollow at first, later filled with evanescent asci ; interior powdery at maturity, surface smooth to coarsely scaly. Sp brown, globose, ornamented. Ectotrophic. 0335110 Eurotiales (Elaphomyces). 0
0 3b : Frb an apothecium or a hypogeous tuber-like cleistothecium, solid at first and with persistent asci. Sp versiform, smooth or ornamented ; interior never powdery at maturity ; sapro- or ectotrophic.03361204
0s"Pezizales." 4a : Asci operculate in taxa with active spore dispersal. Frb a short-lived apothecium, a tuber-like cleistothecium with passive spore dispersal aided by animals or rarely absent. Sp often large, ellipsoid to globose and often ornamented ; ascus walls amyloid or non-amyloid. Many soil and dung inhabiting saprophitic species, but some ectotrophic. 0467130 Pezizales. 155
0 4b : Asci inoperculate. Frb a short- or long-lived apothecium. Sp tiny to large, of various form ; ascus walls non-amyloid, apical apparatus amyloid or non-amyloid. Saprotrophic, parasitic or rarely ectotrophic.04681405
0s"Rhytismatales (Rhytismataceae)." 5a : Frb formed within host tissue or within a black sclerotium-like stroma formed within host tissue, variously shaped, often slit-like or splitting host surface in a stellate or irregular fashion ; in some spp. the apothecia develop in spring on overwintered stromata. Sp phaseoliform to filiform, 1- to multi-celled ; ascus apical structure poroid ; paraphyses much branched apically or curled at the tip. Saprophitic or parasitic. 0589150 Rhytismatales (Rhytismataceae). 258
0 5b : Frb formed outside host tissue or erumpent, cup-, disc-, club-shaped or resembling a corticioid fungus. Sp of various form.058101606
0s"Neolectales (Neolecta)." 6a : Paraphyses and croziers absent. Frb clavate. Ascus wall amyloid after KOH treatment ; sp reniform, producing phialoconidia, hyaline ; ascus apex thickened, with narrow pore. Associated with conifer roots (parasitic ?). 061011170 Neolectales (Neolecta). 0
0 6b : Paraphyses present, if absent then frb tiny, with very few asci. Frb variously shaped. Ascus wall non-amyloid ; apical apparatus absent or pore-like, amyloid or non-amyloid.0610121807
0s"Erysiphales (Thelebolaceae)." 7a : Asci dehiscing with a slit, without operculum or internal pore-like structure, sometimes with subapical annular thickening, saccate, from 1- to often polysporous ; sp ellipsoid, smooth, hyaline. Frb simple apothecia or hardly developed in one genus, short-lived ; coprophilous saprotrophs. 071213190 Erysiphales (Thelebolaceae). 14
0s"Leotiales." 7b : Asci not dehiscing slit-like, often with distinct internal pore-like structure ; sp ellipsoid, fusoid or filiform. Frb discoid, cupulate, turbinate, clavate, etc., often relatively long lived and firm textured, some develop from sclerotia ; many litter inhabiting species, saprotrophic, parasitic or rarely ectotrophic. 071214200 Leotiales. 42
0s"Onygenales (Onygena)." 8a : Frb a stipitate cleistothecium. Asci spherical, deliquesching. Saprotrophs on hoofs, horns and feathers. 08415210 Onygenales (Onygena). 0
0 8b : Frb a perithecium, either solitary or enclosed in stroma. Asci unitunicate, mostly cylindric, persistent, typically with an apical apparatus. On a range of substrates but not on hoofs, horns and feathers.084162209
0s"Hypocreales." 9a : Frb never carbonized, often with brown, yellow or red colours ; stroma when present soft and fleshy. Paraphyses not present at maturity ; asci with non-amyloid apical apparatus ; sp often hyaline to pale brown, ornamented and 2-celled, never with germ apparatus. Saprotrophic or parasitic on plants, insects or fungi. 091617230 Hypocreales. 18
0 9b : Frb carbonized or if not then maturing in living leaves ; stroma, when present, mostly with firm texture. True paraphyses present, asci with amyloid or non-amyloid apical apparatus ; sp hyaline to opaque brown, smooth or ornamented, often with appendages and some with a pore or slit-like germ apparatus. Saprotrophic or parasitic on plants.09161824010
0s"Diatrypales (Diatrype)." 10a : Asci typically very long stipitate with allantoid sp arranged more or less biseriately or irregularly ; apical apparatus diminutive, amyloid or nor ; anamorphs typically coelomycetous. 0101819250 Diatrypales (Diatrype). 0
0 10b : Asci not long stipitate or sp shaped differently.010182026011
0s"Phyllachorales (Polystigma)." 11a : Parasitic on leaves of Rosaceae ; stroma immersed beneath epidermis in living leaves, in shades of orange. Asci clavate ; sp ellipsoid, 1-celled, smooth, hyaline to yellowish. Stromata harden and blacken after leaf fall and the perithecia are fully mature in spring. 0112021270 Phyllachorales (Polystigma). 257
0 11b : Not parasitic on Rosaceae and with orange stromata.011202228012
0s"Sordariales (Camarops)." 12a : Sp inconspicuously terminally bi-porous, 1-celled, smoky grey or olive ; ascus apparatus minute, non-amyloid. Perithecia aggregated in small to very big, ± erumpent stromata, arranged mono- or polysticuously. Saprotrophic or parasitic on deciduous trees and conifers. 0122223290 Sordariales (Camarops). 0
0 12b : Sp not terminally bi-porous, 1-celled or with hyaline dwarf cell (primary appendage) ; apical apparatus amyloid, dextrinoid or unstained.012222430013
0s"Phyllachorales (Phyllachora)." 13a : Sp hyaline to yellowish without germ apparatus ; apical apparatus inamyloid. Frb immersed beneath blackened clypeus. Anamorphs coelomycetous. Parasitic on herbs including grasses (note that a range of pyrenomycetes, e.g. belonging to the Diaporthales will key out here, but they are not included in this work). 0132425310 Phyllachorales (Phyllachora). 257
0s"Xylariales (Xylariaceae)." 13b : Sp grey, olive brown or nearly black, with longitudinal germ slits, rarely without or with poroid, non-terminal germ apparatus ; apical apparatus normally amyloid or dextrinoid. Stromata present, typically as flattened or pulvinate crusts, or erect club-shaped or filiform ; when stroma clypeoid then sp either brown and/or apical apparatus amyloid ; anamorphs when present usually hyphomycetous. Saprotrophic or more rarely necrotrophic or parasitic. 0132426320 Xylariales (Xylariaceae). 260
0 Erysiphales GWYNNER-VAUGHAN - Thelebolaceae (BRUMM.) ECKBLAD0-10273400
0s"Ascozonus."  1a : Asci with 8-64 sp, sp 11.5-13 x 3.5-6 µm. 0141328360 Ascozonus. 0
0 1b : Asci with more sp and/or sp smaller.014132937015
0 2a : Asci with 8 sp.015293038016
0 2b : Asci with 32-7000 sp.015293139017
0s"Pseudoascozonus." 3a : Apothecia c. 0.1 mm, without excipulum. 0163032400 Pseudoascozonus. 0
0s"Thelebolus p.p." 3b : Apothecia c. 0.5-1 mm, with excipulum. 0163033410 Thelebolus p.p. 0
0s"Trichobolus." 4a : Apothecia with stiff, pointed hairs. 0173134420 Trichobolus. 0
0s"Thelebolus." 4b : Apothecia glabrous. 0173135430 Thelebolus. 0
0 Hypocreales LINDAU0-20364500
0s"Clavicipitaceae." 1a : Sp filiform or almost so, mostly multiseptate ; asci with distinct apical crown. 0181737470 Clavicipitaceae. 19
0s"Hypocreaceae." 1b : Sp globose, ellipsoid to cylindric, 1-septate or more rarely aseptate or with several septa ; asci with simple apical pores or without apparent apical apparatus. 0181738480 Hypocreaceae. 22
0 Clavicipitaceae (LINDAU) EARLE ex ROGERSON0-30395000
0 1a : Parasitic on fungi incl. lichenized fungi and insects.019374052020
0 1b : Parasitic on inflorescences of Poaceae and Cyperaceae.019374153021
0s"Neobarya." 2a : Parasitic on Bertia moriformis, Claviceps-sclerotia or Cladonia-thalli ; perithecia united or not in fleshy stromata. 0204042540 Neobarya. 0
0s"Cordyceps." 2b : Parasitic on insects or Elaphomyces ; perithecia united in fleshy stromata. 0204043550 Cordyceps. 0
0s"Epichloe." 3a : Stromata sheathing living culms of Poaceae in late summer ; first white and anamorphic then straw coloured with immersed Perithecia. 0214144560 Epichloe. 0
0s"Claviceps." 3b : Perithecia immersed in capitate, purplish, stipitate stromata, developed from sclerotia in early summer ; sclerotia developed in late summer and autumn. 0214145570 Claviceps. 0
0 Hypocreaceae DE NOT. s.l.0-40465900
0s"Heleococcum." 1a : Frb a cleistothecium containing orange sp in globose asci. 0223847610 Heleococcum. 0
0 1b : Frb a perithecium, non-stromatic or seated upon or contained within a stroma or subiculum. Asci clavate to cylindric, sp of various coulours or hyaline.022384862023
0 2a : Sp with more than one septum.023484963024
0 2b : Sp without or with one septum.023485064031
0 3a : Sp muriform.024495165025
0 3b : Sp only transversely septate.024495266026
0s"Nectria p.p." 4a : Sp without cilia. Perithecia in dense clusters on Berberis or Ribes. 0255153670 Nectria p.p. 0
0s"Paranectria p.p." 4b : Sp ciliate. Perithecia superficial on lichen-thalli. 0255154680 Paranectria p.p. 0
0s"Gibberella." 5a : Perithecia appearing black but dark blue in transmitted light. 0265255690 Gibberella. 0
0 5b : Perithecia in shades of yellow and red, never black or blue.026525670027
0s"Trichonectria." 6a : Perithecia with hyaline, thick-walled hairs. 0275657710 Trichonectria. 0
0 6b : Perithecia not with such hairs.027565872028
0s"Nectria p.p." 7a : On conifer bark ; perithecia conspicuous, red. 0285859730 Nectria p.p. 0
0 7b : On leaf litter, lichen- and algae-thalli, etc.028586074029
0s"Calonectria." 8a : On leaf litter, rarely on woody substrates. Sp 3-5-septate, 40-80 µm long. Perithecia superficial. 0296061750 Calonectria. 0
0 8b : On lichen- or algae-thalli. Perithecia immersed or superficial.029606276030
0s"Pronectria p.p." 9a : Sp without cilia. Perithecia completely immersed, only ostiole erumpent. On lichen- or algae-thalli. 0306263770 Pronectria p.p. 0
0s"Paranectria p.p." 9b : Sp ciliate. Perithecia superficial. On lichen-thalli. 0306264780 Paranectria p.p. 0
0s"Selinia." 10a : Sp non-septate, fusoid, thick-walled, smooth, more than 40 µm long. On dung. 0315065790 Selinia. 0
0 10b : Sp septate or if non-septate with other shapes or ornamentations. Not on dung.031506680032
0 11a : Sp at maturity breaking into part sp.032666781033
0 11b : Sp not breaking into part sp at maturity.032666882034
0s"Arachnocrea." 12a : Part sp acutely pointed to apiculate. Stromata arachnoid, very thin. 0336769830 Arachnocrea. 0
0s"Hypocrea." 12b : Part sp normally with rounded ends. Stromata spongy and loose to firm with distinct rind. 0336770840 Hypocrea. 710
0 See also Podostroma.0336771850N0
0s"Hypocreopsis." 13a : Stromata with fingerlike outgrowths. Parasitic on Hymenochaete. 0346872860 Hypocreopsis. 0
0 13b : Stromata either absent, pulvinate or effused without finger-like outgrowths. Not associated with Hymenochaete.034687387035
0 14a : Stromata developing on fungi or on a thin subiculum. Sp ± fusoid.035737488036
0 14b : Stromata, if present, developing on other substrate or sp with different shape.035737589038
0s"Hypomyces." 15a : Sp > 15 µm, densely verrucose, often with distinct apiculi ; anamorphs in Cladobotryum, Mycogone, Papulospora, Pseudohansfordia, Sepedonium and Sibirina. 0367476900 Hypomyces. 0
0 15b : Sp < 15 µm long, never apiculate.036747791037
0s"Nectriopsis." 16a : On both myxomycetes and fungi ; anamorphs Acremonium-like. 0377778920 Nectriopsis. 0
0s"Sphaerostilbella." 16b : On Stereum, anamorphs in Gliocladium. 0377779930 Sphaerostilbella. 0
0 17a : Perithecia superficial, with or without a basal stroma.038758094039
0 17b : Perithecia immersed, erumpent or not.038758195041
0s"Bryonectria." 18a : Perithecia hyaline or whitish. On Hylocomium. 0398082960 Bryonectria. 0
0 18b : Perithecia more colourful or host different.039808397040
0s"Nectria p.p." 19a : Perithecia smooth or scurfy, rarely hairy, stromata often developed underneath. Sp 2-celled. On all kind of substrates. 0408384980 Nectria p.p. 0
0s"Pseudonectria." 19b : Perithecia more or less hairy, no obvious stroma present. Sp aseptate. On leaves of Buxus. 0408385990 Pseudonectria. 0
0s"Pronectria." 20a : On lichenized fungi and Laminaria-thalli. 04181861000 Pronectria. 0
0s"Nectriella." 20b : On other substrates. 04181871010 Nectriella. 0
0 Leotiales S.E.CARP.0-508810300
0s"Ascocorticiaceae." 1a : Frb a very thin, whitish mat, a few mm in diam. On bark (often inner side) of Pinus. 04214891050 Ascocorticiaceae. 52
0 1b : Frb with a more distinct shape.0421490106043
0s"Vibrisseaceae (Vibrissea)." 2a : Sp hyaline, filiform, very long, breaking into numerous part-sp, 1-2.5 µm thick. In springs. 04390911070 Vibrisseaceae (Vibrissea). 0
0 2b : Sp hyaline or coloured ; if very long then not breaking apart or thicker than 3 µm.0439092108044
0 3a : Apothecia arising from a stroma or sclerotium, or from stromatised host tissue.0449293109045
0 3b : Apothecia not with the above characters.0449294110046
0s"Sclerotiniaceae." 4a : Apothecia cupulate, arising distinct sclerotia or stroma with a well differentiated rind and medulla. Obligatory or facultative parasites. Sp unicellular. 04593951110 Sclerotiniaceae. 145
0s"Rutstroemiaceae." 4b : Apothecia cupulate or campanulate, arising from an indeterminate brown to black crust-like stroma or stromatal host tissue with or without a rind. Mainly saprotrophs. Sp uni- or multicellular. 04593961120 Rutstroemiaceae. 142
0s"Hyaloscyphaceae." 5a : Apothecia subsessile or stipitate, disc-shaped or cup-shaped ; outside covered with white or coloured hairs. On leaves, herbaceous stems or wood. 04694971130 Hyaloscyphaceae. 62
0 5b : Apothecia not with the above combinations of characters.0469498114047
0 6a : Frb distinctly stipitate.0479899115048
0 6b : Frb sessile or subsessile.04798100116050
0s"Leotiaceae." 7a : Apothecia convex and lobed, clavate, hemispheric or globose, or disc-shaped to cup-shaped, margin free of stem. 048991011170 Leotiaceae. 91
0 7b : Apothecia clavate, spathulate or capitate, with no abrupt or definite margin between hymenium and stem.04899102118049
0s"Geoglossaceae." 8a : Paraphyses present. 0491021031190 Geoglossaceae. 54
0s"Neolectales." 8b : Paraphyses absent. Frb with white to yellowish stem and yellow hymenium. 0491021041200 Neolectales. 0
0s"Dermateaceae." 9a : Apothecia disc-shaped, margin even or torn, outside often dark brownish. Flesh soft, composed of angular or subglobose cells. 0501001051210 Dermateaceae. 53
0 9b : Apothecia disc-shaped, cup-shaped or turbinate ; margin even or delicately dentate ; outside often concolorous with the hymenium. Flesh tough, leathery or gelatinous.050100106122051
0s"Orbiliaceae." 10a : Frb disc-shaped, sessile, 1-2 mm, waxy, light-coloured and hyaline when fresh. Asci and paraphyses adherent ; paraphyses capitate. 0511061071230 Orbiliaceae. 141
0s"Leotiaceae." 10b : Frb variously shaped, sessile or stipitate, small or large, rarely hyaline. Asci and paraphyses not adherent. 0511061081240 Leotiaceae. 91
0 Ascocorticiaceae J.SCHRÖT.0-6010912600
0s"Ascocorticium." 1a : Sp ellipsoid, aseptate ; asci cylindric, 8-spored. 052891101280 Ascocorticium. 0
0s"Ascocorticiellum." 1b : Sp vermiform, 3-septate ; asci broadly clavate, 16-spored. 052891111290 Ascocorticiellum. 0
0 Dermateaceae FR.0-7011213100
0s"Podophacidium." 1a : On soil or plant debris. Apothecia turbinate to cup-shaped, hymenium bright yellow ; margin dentate ; outside dark brown to black. 0531051131330 Podophacidium. 0
0s"Mollisia." 1b : On wood of deciduous trees. Apothecia disc-shaped, hymenium greyish or yellowish grey, margin nearly white, even ; outside brownish. 0531051141340 Mollisia. 0
0 Geoglossaceae CORDA0-8011513600
0 1a : Frb clavate, black or brown.054103116138055
0 1b : Frb clavate or compressed, yellow, ochraceous or green.054103117139058
0 2a : Sp persistently hyaline.055116118140056
0 2b : Sp brown at maturity.055116119141057
0s"Geoglossum." 3a : Frb black or dark purplish. 0561181201420 Geoglossum. 0
0s"Microglossum." 3b : Frb pale brown to reddish brown. 0561181211430 Microglossum. 0
0s"Geoglossum." 4a : Setae absent. 0571191221440 Geoglossum. 0
0s"Trichoglossum." 4b : Brown setae present (frb hairy, use lens !). 0571191231450 Trichoglossum. 0
0s"Microglossum." 5a : Frb ± green. 0581171241460 Microglossum. 0
0 5b : Frb yellow or ochraceous.058117125147059
0 6a : Sp filiform, finally septate.059125126148060
0 6b : Sp fusoid.059125127149061
0s"Spathularia." 7a : Frb spathulate, with laterally compressed hymenium. 0601261281500 Spathularia. 0
0s"Cudonia." 7b : Frb capitate, with rounded hymenium. 0601261291510 Cudonia. 0
