0s"Myriosclerotinia." 4a : Sclerotia borne within stems of juncaceous and cyperaceous hosts, sclerotia cylindric to tuberoid. Macroconidial state unknown (see also Sclerotinia tetraspora). 01483063093410 Myriosclerotinia. 0
0 4b : Sclerotia formed on leaves, stems and roots of other plants, wholly or partially embedded in and digesting host tissues ; sclerotial medulla with remnants of host tissues, or with a gelatinous substance between sclerotial hyphae.01483063103420149
0s"Ovulinia." 5a : Sclerotia discoid ; on wilting flowers (petals) of Rhododendron. Macroconidia borne on short conidiophores (form genus Ovulitis). 01493103113430 Ovulinia. 0
0s"Botryotinia." 5b : Sclerotia pyramidal, discoid or flat ; on stems, leaves or rhizomes. Macroconidia borne on straight, branched conidiophores (form genus Botrytis). 01493103123440 Botryotinia. 0
0 6a : Stroma a black crust-like stroma with a well differentiated rind.01503043133450151
0 6b : Stroma consisting of areas of stromatized (blackened) host tissues with or without an obvious stromatal rind.01503043143460153
0s"Monilinia." 7a : Stroma crusty, black, mummified, formed within fruits of ericaceous and rosaceous hosts. Macroconidial state on leaves or fruits ; macroconidia borne in monilioid chains separated by disjunctors or not (form genus Monilia). 01513133153470 Monilinia. 0
0 7b : Stroma not as above.01513133163480152
0s"Stromatinia." 8a : Stroma a blackened, mantling stroma of indefinite dimensions developed on rhizomes and bulbs of monocotyledons. Macroconidial state absent. 01523163173490 Stromatinia. 0
0s"Valdensinia." 8b : Stroma an indefinite, crust-like stroma ; on leaves of Vaccinium myrtillus. Conidial anamorph with four-armed diasporas (form genus Valdensia), ca. 0.5 mm diam. 01523163183500 Valdensinia. 0
0s"Encoelia." 9a : Sp ± allantoid. On wood. 01533143193510 Encoelia. 0
0 9b : Sp ± ellipsoid. On leaves, catkins, fruits, bulbils.01533143203520154
0s"Pycnopeziza." 10a : Apothecia short-stipitate, at first closed and ‘cup-shaped’, then expanding and radially splitting in a stellate manner, hymenium pale yellowish brown, outside brownish black ; on leaves and branchlets. Macroconidial state borne in pycnidia-like organs, consisting of arthroconidia in chains on branches on the host (form genus Acarosporium). 01543203213530 Pycnopeziza. 0
0s"Ciboria." 10b : Apothecia regularly cup-shaped, hymenium and receptacle concolorous. 01543203223540 Ciboria. 0
0 Pezizales BESSEY0-14032335600
0 1a : Frb in soil, hypogeous or nearly so, closed or with one to several small apical openings. Spore liberation passive.015573243580156
0 1b : Frb epigeous ; on soil, wood or dung. At maturity with free hymenium or asci protruding. Spore liberation active.015573253590161
0 2a : Frb solid, ± regularly tuber-like, with veined gleba and well defined peridium, with or without rhizoids on the lower side.01563243263600157
0 2b : Frb ± hollow, often strongly folded and with several smaller or larger interior lacunes, in some spp. with a small, central opening on the upper side, often irregular in shape and/or with thin, ill defined peridium.01563243273610159
0s"Pezizaceae (Pachyphloeus)" 3a : Frb with small depression on the upper side and rhizoids on the lower side, usually < 2 cm. Asci amyloid, at least at apex, 8-spored ; sp ornamented. 01573263283620 Pezizaceae (Pachyphloeus). 184
0 3b : Frb without specific depression on the upper side, with or without rhizoids on the lower side, often > 2 cm. Asci non-amyloid, 1-8-spored, sp ornamented or smooth.01573263293630158
0s"Helvellaceae." 4a : Sp ellipsoid and smooth or > 50 µm long and verrucose. 01583293303640 Helvellaceae. 178
0s"Tuberaceae." 4b : Sp ornamented and if > 50 µm long then with a reticulate ornamentation. 01583293313650 Tuberaceae. 256
0s"Helvellaceae (Helvella astieri)." 5a : Frb grey, pubescent, mostly epigeous, closed, ± hollow and strongly folded inside. Sp ellipsoid, smooth. 01593273323660 Helvellaceae (Helvella astieri). 178
0 5b : Frb different.01593273333670160
0s"Pyronemataceae p.p." 6a : Sp smooth or if ornamented then frb ± cup-shaped with a central opening on top and folded-hollow inside. 01603333343680 Pyronemataceae p.p. 191
0s"Discinaceae p.p." 6b : Sp ornamented. Frb with very irregular outline or strongly folded inside, reddish brown or becoming red when sectioned. 01603333353690 Discinaceae p.p. 175
0 7a : Asci amyloid, at least at apex.01613253363700162
0 7b : Asci non-amyloid.01613253373710163
0s"Ascobolaceae." 8a : Apothecia whitish, yellowish, greyish, with bluish or purplish tinge, usually 0.1-12 mm broad, pulvinate, disc-shaped or turbinate. Sp hyaline or purplish, globose or ellipsoid, smooth or ornamented, without guttules. Often on dung. 01623363383720 Ascobolaceae. 173
0s"Pezizaceae p.p." 8b : Apothecia greyish, brownish, greenish, bluish, purplish or black, usually 1-8 cm broad, pulvinate, disc-shaped or cup-shaped. Sp hyaline to pale brownish, globose, ellipsoid or fusoid, smooth or ornamented, with or without guttules. 01623363393730 Pezizaceae p.p. 184
0s"Sarcoscyphaceae." 9a : Apothecia either sessile, orange and on needles or twigs of Juniperus, Abies or Picea, or stipitate with scarlet hymenium and on ± buried twigs and branches. Spring. 01633373403740 Sarcoscyphaceae. 249
0 9b : Apothecia not with the above combination of characters.01633373413750164
0s"Sarcosomataceae." 10a : Apothecia either 0.5-12 cm broad, with dark brown to black hymenium, cup-shaped, subglobose, infundibuliform or urceolate, with greyish, brownish to black, glabrous, wrinkled to folded or hairy outside or apothecia 0.1-0.3 cm broad, whitish, disc-shaped with long brown hairs, on needles of Pinus. Early spring to summer. 01643413423760 Sarcosomataceae. 251
0 10b : Apothecia not with the above combination of characters.01643413433770165
0 11a : On dung of carnivorous or herbivorous animals or birds. Apothecia whitish, yellowish or brownish, with a distinct excipulum. Asci with 8-7000 hyaline sp. 01653433443780 See Thelebolaceae.0
0 11b : Apothecia not with the above combination of characters.01653433453790166
0 12a : Apothecia from early spring to early summer, one spp. in autumn ; often stipitate or substipitate, several cm high and broad, often thick-fleshed (> 2 mm), yellow brown, brown to blackish brown. Sp with prominent appendages at the poles or smooth and globose or ellipsoid. On soil or wood.01663453463800167
0 12b : Apothecia in autumn or if in spring then smaller, of another colour and more thin-fleshed (< 2 mm).01663453473810168
0s"Morchellaceae." 13a : Most spp. with a campanulate, even or wrinkled, sponge-like or honeycomb-like ‘cap’ and a ± hollow, whitish stem, longer than cap, one sp. substipitate, cup-shaped, fragile, 3-12 cm broad and with a smell of chlorine when broken ; apothecia (1)-2-8 cm broad and 4-20 cm high. Sp smooth, ellipsoid, sp-print yellowish. On soil. 01673463483820 Morchellaceae. 182
0s"Discinaceae." 13b : Apothecia with an irregular, saddle-shaped or brain-like folded ‘cap’ or cup-shaped and substipitate, 2-12 cm broad, 2-12 cm high, no smell of chlorine when broken ; stem generally shorter than ‘cap’ high. Sp with prominent appendages at the poles or smooth, ellipsoid or globose ; sp-print whitish. On soil, trunks or stumps. 01673463493830 Discinaceae. 175
0 14a : Apothecia ear-shaped.01683473503840169
0 14b : Apothecia pulvinate, disc-shaped or cup-shaped.01683473513850170
0s"Helvellaceae (Wynnella)." 15a : Apothecia blood-red to reddish brown, outside glabrous. Sp broadly ellipsoid with one large guttule. 01693503523860 Helvellaceae (Wynnella). 178
0s"Pyronemataceae p.p." 15b : Apothecia yellowish, orange, ochraceous or brownish, sometimes with olivaceous, pinkish or reddish tinge. Sp narrowly ellipsoid with two small guttules. 01693503533870 Pyronemataceae p.p. 191
0 16a : Apothecia pulvinate, chestnut, 4-15 cm broad, with numerous rhizoids. Sp fusoid, apiculate, with delicate, reticulate ornamentation. On burnt ground ; autumn. 01703513543880 Rhizinaceae (Rhizina).0
0 16b : Apothecia not with the above combination of characters.01703513553890171
0s"Helvellaceae p.p." 17a : Apothecia medium to large or if small then black, subsessile to stipitate, cup-shaped, saddle-shaped to irregularly saddle-shaped ; hymenium brownish, greyish or black ; outside glabrous or pubescent. Sp broadly ellipsoid, rarely fusoid, typically with one large guttule. On mull or calcareous soil ; spring to autumn. 01713553563900 Helvellaceae p.p. 178
0 17b : Apothecia very small to medium, sessile or substipitate.01713553573910172
0 18a : Apothecia membranous, 3-12 mm in diam., brownish red, paler towards the margin. Excipulum of interwoven hyphae ; sp 12-15 x 5.5-7 µm, ellipsoid, smooth, without guttules. Spring to early summer. 01723573583920 See Karstenellaceae (Karstenella).0
0s"Pyronemataceae p.p." 18b : Apothecia not with the above combination of characters, fleshy, rarely hypogeous, pulvinate, disc-shaped or cup-shaped ; hymenium whitish, greyish, yellowish, orange, reddish, bluish or purplish ; outside glabrous, furfuraceous or hairy. Sp hyaline or pale brownish or purplish, globose, ellipsoid or fusoid, with or without guttules, smooth or ornamented. Spring to autumn. 01723573593930 Pyronemataceae p.p. 191
0 Ascobolaceae BOUD. ex SACC.0-15036039500
0 1a : Sp hyaline, then purplish to reddish violet ; asci with 8 free sp or sp united in a cluster.01733383613970174
0s"Thecotheus." 1b : Sp permanently hyaline ; asci with 8-32 free sp, ellipsoid, thick-walled, smooth or ornamented, with apiculi at the poles, with thick gelatinous coating. On dung. 01733383623980 Thecotheus. 0
0s"Ascobolus." 2a : Apothecia globose, turbinate or disc-shaped, 0.2-8-(12) mm broad, whitish, yellow or pale brownish, then often purplish brown. Sp free, ellipsoid or globose, smooth or ornamented, often with gelatinous coating. On dung, herbaceous stems, soil or burnt ground. 01743613633990 Ascobolus. 0
0s"Saccobolus." 2b : Apothecia globose, turbinate or pulvinate, 0.1-1 mm broad, whitish with purplish tinge or yellow. Sp united in one cluster, smooth or ornamented, with unilateral or universal gelatinous coating. On dung. 01743613644000 Saccobolus. 0
0 Discinaceae BENEDIX0-16036540200
0 1a : Frb epigeous.01753493664040176
0 1b : Frb hypogeous.01753493674050177
0s"Gyromitra." 2a : Frb saddle-shaped to cerebriform, reddish brown to dark brown, often with a purplish tinge, stipitate. Sp smooth, narrowly ellipsoid and with 2 small guttules or globose. 01763663684060 Gyromitra. 0
0s"Discina." 2b : Frb disc-shaped or cerebriform, brownish, subsessile or stipitate. Sp broadly ellipsoid, apiculate, when mature with a reticulate ornamentation and 3-4 large guttules. 01763663694070 Discina. 0
0s"Hydnobolites." 3a : Sp 20-25 µm in diam., with a reticulate ornamentation. 01773673704080 Hydnobolites. 0
0s"Hydnotrya." 3b : Sp 22-40 µm in diam., verrucose. 01773673714090 Hydnotrya. 0
0 Helvellaceae FR. (Incl. Balsamiaceae E.Fisch.)0-17037241100
0 1a : Frb epigeous.01783563734130179
0 1b : Frb hypogeous.01783563744140181
0s"Pindara." 2a : Frb 3-6 mm broad, purplish blanc. 01793733754150 Pindara. 0
0 2b : Frb larger.01793733764160180
0s"Helvella." 3a : Frb cup-shaped to saddle-shaped, hymenium white, greyish, brownish or black, subsessile to distinctly stipitate. 01803763774170 Helvella. 0
0s"Wynnella." 3b : Frb rabbit-ear shaped, subsessile or with a short narrow stem. 01803763784180 Wynnella. 0
0s"Balsamia." 4a : Sp smooth, 17-24 µm long. 01813743794190 Balsamia. 0
0s"Fischerula." 4b : Sp verrucose, 55-69 µm long. 01813743804200 Fischerula. 0
0 Morchellaceae REICHENB.0-18038142200
0s"Disciotis." 1a : Sessile or subsessile, cup-shaped to expanded, inside wrinkled to folded, 3-12 cm broad ; flesh with smell of chlorine. 01823483824240 Disciotis. 0
0 1b : Distinctly stipitate ; smell faint.01823483834250183
0s"Verpa." 2a : Apothecia campanulate, 1.5-3 cm high, even or with irregular or longitudinal furrows or ribs. Asci with 2 or 8 sp. 01833833844260 Verpa. 0
0s"Morchella." 2b : Apothecia sponge-like or honeycomb-like, 2-10 cm high. Asci with 8 sp. 01833833854270 Morchella. 0
0 Pezizaceae DUMORT.0-19038642900
0 1a : Sp ellipsoid.01843393874310185
0 1b : Sp globose.01843393884320188
0s"Pachyella." 2a : Excipulum cells embedded in a gel. Apothecia pulvinate ; on wet, sometimes submerged wood. 01853873894330 Pachyella. 0
0 2b : Excipulum cells not embedded in a gel. Apothecia disc-shaped or cup-shaped.01853873904340186
0s"Sarcosphaera." 3a : Apothecia very large, at first hypogeous and globose, then deeply cup-shaped, margin splitting into irregular rays ; hymenium violaceous. 01863903914350 Sarcosphaera. 0
0 3b : Apothecia small to medium, disc-shaped to cup-shaped, epigeous.01863903924360187
0s"Iodophanus." 4a : Apothecia < 3 mm, whitish, yellowish to pale orange. 01873923934370 Iodophanus. 0
0s"Peziza." 4b : Apothecia > 1 mm, typically brown, with shades of violaceous, yellow, green, blue, etc. 01873923944380 Peziza. 0
0s"Pachyphloeus." 5a : Frb hypogeous. 01883883954390 Pachyphloeus. 0
0 5b : Frb epigeous.01883883964400189
0s"Scabropezia." 6a : Hymenium greenish, outer surface of the apothecia prominently pustulate, composed of aggregates of globose to angular cells. On soil and decaying wood. 01893963974410 Scabropezia. 0
0 6b : Hymenium purplish, brownish or black ; outer surface glabrous or furfuraceous. On soil or burnt areas.01893963984420190
0s"Boudiera." 7a : Apothecia pulvinate. Outer excipulum with globose to elongate cells, medullary excipulum of densely interwoven hyphae. On soil, often in recently flooded areas. 01903983994430 Boudiera. 0
0s"Plicaria." 7b : Apothecia disc-shaped to cup-shaped. Outer excipulum of globose cells and intermixed broad hyphae. Often on burnt areas. 01903984004440 Plicaria. 0
0 Pyronemataceae CORDA0-20040144600
0 1a : Frb epigeous.01913594024480192
0 1b : Frb ± hypogeous, ± hollow (see also Geopora).01913594034490248
0 2a : Apothecia on outside with appressed or projecting hairs.01924024044500193
0 2b : Apothecia on outside glabrous or furfuraceous.01924024054510218
0 3a : Hymenium yellowish, orange, pink or red.01934044064520194
0 3b : Hymenium whitish, greyish, ochraceous or brownish.01934044074530206
0 4a : Hairs yellowish, brownish to black.01944064084540195
0 4b : Hairs whitish or hyaline.01944064094550202
0 5a : Hairs appressed, yellowish brown to black, obtuse.01954084104560196
0 5b : Hairs projecting, yellowish to dark brown, pointed.01954084114570198
0s"Ramsbottomia." 6a : Sp globose or subglobose, echinulate. Apothecia disc-shaped, 0.1-0.6 cm, margin indistinct ; hymenium yellowish, orange or red ; outside with short, yellowish brown hairs (lens !). On naked soil or lime. 01964104124580 Ramsbottomia. 0
0 6b : Sp ellipsoid.01964104134590197
0s"Anthracobia." 7a : Apothecia on burnt ground. Sessile, often gregarious, disc-shaped, 0.2-1.2 cm broad ; margin distinct; hymenium yellowish, orange or red ; outside with short brownish hairs. Sp ellipsoid, smooth, with two guttules. 01974134144600 Anthracobia. 0
0s"Melastiza." 7b : Apothecia on soil. Sessile, solitary or gregarious, disc-shaped or cup-shaped, 0.3-2.5 cm broad ; margin distinct ; hymenium orange or red ; outside with adnate, pale brownish to black hairs. Sp ellipsoid, ornamented. 01974134154610 Melastiza. 0
0s"Scutellinia." 8a : Hairs rooting, developing from cells in the medullary excipulum ; apothecia disc-shaped, 0.5-1.5 cm broad ; margin distinct ; hymenium red to scarlet ; outside with pointed, brown or dark brown, 150-200 µm long hairs. Sp ellipsoid, globose or subglobose, ornamented. 01984114164620 Scutellinia. 0
0 8b : Hairs developing form cells in the outer excipulum.01984114174630199
0s"Parascutellinia." 9a : Hymenium red with bluish tinge, apothecia solitary, sessile, low cup-shaped, 3-5 mm broad ; margin distinct ; outside set with 140-600 µm long, multiseptate, brown hairs developing form bulbose cells in outer excipulum. Sp ellipsoid, smooth, with two guttules. In temporarily inundated areas along rivers, ponds, etc. 01994174184640 Parascutellinia. 0
0 9b : Hymenium yellowish, orange or red.01994174194650200
0s"Tricharina." 10a : On limestone or burnt ground ; apothecia sessile, hemispheric to low cup-shaped, 0.5-1 cm broad ; hymenium yellowish, outside concolorous or brownish, with bundles of thin-walled, pale brownish hairs. Sp ellipsoid, smooth. 02004194204660 Tricharina. 0
0 10b : On dung, soil or plant debris.02004194214670201
0s"Cheilymenia." 11a : Hairs ± furcated at the base or stellate ; sp without guttules. 02014214224680 Cheilymenia. 0
0s"Spooneromyces." 11b : Hairs not furcated ; sp with two guttules. 02014214234690 Spooneromyces. 0
0s"Rhodoscypha." 12a : Hymenium pink ; apothecia solitary or in troops, 0.5-1 cm broad, disc-shaped to cup-shaped ; outside whitish, covered by a dense mat of short, white, flexuose hairs. Sp fusoid, 33-46 x 10-16.5 µm, with guttules. On soil or debris. 02024094244700 Rhodoscypha. 0
0 12b : Hymenium yellowish, orange or red. Sp ellipsoid.02024094254710203
0 13a : Hairs slender, like hyphae, obtuse or pointed.02034254264720204
0 13b : Hairs thick-walled, pointed.02034254274730205
0s"Neottiella." 14a : Apothecia cup-shaped, 0.2-1.5 cm broad ; hymenium orange or reddish, margin distinct, narrow ; outside with pointed, narrow, whitish hairs. Sp ellipsoid, ornamented or smooth, with guttules. On sandy soil together with Polytrichum or with Funaria on burnt ground. 02044264284740 Neottiella. 0
0 14b : Apothecia first hemispheric, subimmersed, then disc-shaped, 0.3-1.5 cm broad ; hymenium pale orange or dirty yellowish, margin distinct ; outside with obtuse, short, whitish hairs. Sp ellipsoid to fusoid, with guttules. On naked clayey or calcareous soil. 02044264294750 Pustularia patavina.4300
0 See Tarzetta.02044264304760N0
0s"Lasiobolus." 15a : On dung. Hairs non-septate, thick-walled, pointed ; apothecia 0.2-1 mm broad, turbinate to disc-shaped, yellowish or reddish. Sp ellipsoid, smooth, with gelatinous coating, without guttules. 02054274314770 Lasiobolus. 0
0s"Cheilymenia p.p." 15b : On dung, soil or plant debris. Hairs septate, whitish or brownish ; apothecia 0.5-1.5 cm broad, disc-shaped, margin distinct. 02054274324780 Cheilymenia p.p. 0
0 16a : Hairs brownish.02064074334790207
0 16b : Hairs whitish.02064074344800217
0s"Scutellinia p.p." 17a : Hairs rooting, developing from cells in medullary excipulum. 02074334354810 Scutellinia p.p. 0
0 17b : Hairs developing from cells in outer excipulum.02074334364820208
0s"Geopora." 18a : Apothecia first hypogeous, globose and closed, then splitting in irregular rays, cup-shaped, rarely expanding to disc-shaped, sunken, with margin at soil level ; outside covered by flexuose, brownish hairs. Sp ellipsoid, smooth, with guttules. 02084364374830 Geopora. 0
0 18b : Apothecia epigeous.02084364384840209
0 19a : Hairs projecting, pointed or blunt.02094384394850210
0 19b : Hairs appressed, short or long, straight or flexuose.02094384404860215
0s"Sphaerosporella." 20a : Sp globose. Apothecia turbinate to disc-shaped, 0.2-0.6 cm broad ; margin distinct ; hymenium brownish ; outside brown, covered by short, brownish pointed hairs. On burnt ground or clayey soil. 02104394414870 Sphaerosporella. 0
0 20b : Sp subglobose, ellipsoid or fusoid.02104394424880211
0 21a : Sp with guttules.02114424434890212
0 21b : Sp without guttules.02114424444900213
0s"Humaria." 22a : Apothecia deeply cup-shaped, rarely disc-shaped, 0.5-3 cm broad ; hymenium greyish to greyish yellow, sometimes with pink tinge ; outside covered with stiff, brownish, multiseptate hairs. Sp ellipsoid, ornamented, with two guttules. On rich soil. 02124434454910 Humaria. 0
0s"Trichophaea." 22b : Apothecia disc-shaped to low cup-shaped, 0.2-1.2 cm broad, hymenium greyish white ; outside with scattered hyaline or brownish hairs or groups of hairs. Sp subglobose, ellipsoid or fusoid, smooth or ornamented. On soil or burnt ground. 02124434464920 Trichophaea. 0
0s"Trichophaeopsis." 23a : Hairs long, stiff, some bifurcate with one downward pointing branch, outer excipulum cells in vertical rows. Apothecia 0.5-3 mm broad, turbinate to disc-shaped, margin distinct ; hymenium whitish. Sp smooth. On cow-dung, soil or plant debris. 02134444474930 Trichophaeopsis. 0
0 23b : Hairs simple, outer excipulum cells not in rows.02134444484940214
0s"Tricharina." 24a : Apothecia broadly sessile, partially sunken in the substrate ; hairs only marginal. Excipulum distinctly 2-layered with relatively uniform thickness ; sp almost filling the ascus. 02144484494950 Tricharina. 0
0s"Wilcoxina." 24b : Apothecia sessile, centrally attached ; hairs marginal and all over the outside. Sp in upper half of the ascus only. 02144484504960 Wilcoxina. 0
0s"Pseudombrophila." 25a : Sp without guttules, ellipsoid, smooth or rarely delicately ornamented. Hymenium whitish, yellowish grey or pale ochraceous to darker brownish. 02154404514970 Pseudombrophila. 0
0 25b : Sp with guttules, ± ellipsoid, ornamented or smooth.02154404524980216
0s"Nannfeldtiella." 26a : Hymenium dark brown with violet tinge ; apothecia sessile, disc-shaped, 0.3-2.5 cm broad ; outside tomentose, with flexuose hairs. Sp ornamented. Usually in association with the orange Byssonectria terrestris. 02164524534990 Nannfeldtiella. 0
0s"Anthracobia." 26b : Hymenium greyish brown or dark brownish ; apothecia 0.2-1.2 cm broad, sessile, disc-shaped, gregarious; outside with short, straight, appressed hairs. Sp smooth, with two guttules. On burnt ground. 02164524545000 Anthracobia. 0
0 27a : On dung. Apothecia subimmersed, globose or subglobose, whitish or pale yellowish brown, 0.2-0.5 mm broad ; hairs stiff, pointed, 1-10 septate. With one to 3 asci each containing 1500-1700 sp. 02174344555010 See Trichobolus.0
0s"Leucoscypha." 27b : On acid soil. Apothecia superficial, disc-shaped, white all over, 0.2-1 cm broad ; hairs white, multiseptate. Asci with 8 fusoid, ornamented sp. 02174344565020 Leucoscypha. 0
0 28a : Hymenium yellowish, orange, pink or red.02184054575030219
0 28b : Hymenium whitish, greyish, ochraceous, brown or purplish.02184054585040235
0 29a : Apothecia membranous or pulvinate to disc-shaped, margin indistinct or lacking.02194574595050220
0 29b : Apothecia disc-shaped, cup-shaped or ear-shaped.02194574605060228
0s"Pyronema." 30a : On burnt ground or on otherwise sterilized soil. Apothecia densely gregarious on whitish mycelium, turbinate to pulvinate, 1-2 mm broad ; hymenium pink or reddish. Sp ellipsoid, smooth, without guttules. 02204594615070 Pyronema. 0
0 30b : On soil, limestone, dung, plant debris or wood.02204594625080221
0 31a : On soil or limestone.02214624635090222
0 31b : On dung, plant debris or wood.02214624645100223
0s"Pulvinula p.p." 32a : Sp globose or ellipsoid, with guttules ; paraphyses filiform, curved above. Apothecia 0.2-1 cm broad ; hymenium yellowish, orange or red. 02224634655110 Pulvinula p.p. 0
0s"Kotlabaea." 32b : Sp ellipsoid, with many guttules (“spumose”) ; paraphyses straight. Apothecia 1-2 mm broad ; hymenium yellowish orange. 02224634665120 Kotlabaea. 0
0 33a : On dung.02234644675130224
0 33b : On plant debris or wood.02234644685140226
0s"Coprobia." 34a : Sp ellipsoid, very delicately longitudinally striate (oil imm.) ; paraphyses stout, enlarged above to 12-15 µm broad. Apothecia 0.2-1 cm broad, hymenium orange ; outside yellowish white, furfuraceous. 02244674695150 Coprobia. 0
0 34b : Sp ellipsoid, smooth ; paraphyses slender, straight or curved above.02244674705160225
0s"Coprotus p.p." 35a : Sp with conspicuous de Bary bubbles ; paraphyses straight, filiform or curved above. Apothecia yellow or orange, pulvinate to disc-shaped, 0.1-1 mm broad. 02254704715170 Coprotus p.p. 0
0 35b : Sp without de Bary bubbles ; paraphyses straight, enlarged above. Apothecia yellow or yellowish brown, pulvinate to disc-shaped, 0.05-1 mm broad. 02254704725180 See Thelebolus.0
0s"Byssonectria." 36a : Apothecia on plant debris and leaves, in places where animals urinate, in Norway, Sweden and Finland often associated with Nannfeldtiella. Apothecia gregarious on a whitish mat of mycelium (subiculum), 0.5-3 mm broad ; hymenium orange ; outside glabrous. Sp fusoid with guttules, smooth. 02264684735190 Byssonectria. 0
0 36b : Apothecia on wood or soil.02264684745200227
0s"Miladina p.p." 37a : Apothecia pulvinate, 0.5-1 cm broad, yellowish, orange or ochraceous. Sp broadly ellipsoid, verruculose, with many guttules. On wet wood. 02274744755210 Miladina p.p. 0
0 37b : Apothecia thin, membranous, 0.3-1.2 cm broad, brownish red, paler towards the margin, which is orange or greenish yellow in young specimens. Sp ellipsoid, smooth without guttules. 02274744765220 See Karstenella.0
0s"Otidea p.p." 38a : Apothecia split down on one side or ear-shaped, sessile or stipitate, yellow, ochraceous, orange or pink, whitish near the pubescent base of stem. Sp ± ellipsoid, with two guttules, smooth ; paraphyses often hooked. 02284604775230 Otidea p.p. 0
0 38b : Apothecia disc-shaped or cup-shaped.02284604785240229
0s"Sowerbyella." 39a : Apothecia with ± rooting stem, fulvous, orange, yellow or greenish yellow, low cup-shaped, 0.5-5 cm broad ; stem 1-5 cm long, encrusted with debris. Sp ellipsoid, ornamented. 02294784795250 Sowerbyella. 0
0 39b : Apothecia sessile, yellowish, orange, pink or red.02294784805260230
0 40a : Sp globose or subglobosse.02304804815270231
0 40b : Sp ellipsoid or fusoid.02304804825280232
0s"Caloscypha." 41a : Apothecia cup-shaped, 0.5-4 cm broad ; hymenium orange ; outside olivaceous orange, often blue-tinged ; greenish or bluish all over when touched. Sp smooth. 02314814835290 Caloscypha. 0
0s"Lamprospora." 41b : Apothecia disc-shaped, 1-2 mm broad ; hymenium yellow, orange or red, margin distinct, dentate or fimbriate. Sp ornamented. 02314814845300 Lamprospora. 0
0s"Rhodotarzetta." 42a : Apothecia cup-shaped, pink, 0.5-1.2 cm broad. Sp ellipsoid, smooth, with 2 guttules. On burnt ground. 02324824855310 Rhodotarzetta. 0
0 42b : Apothecia yellowish, orange or reddish. On soil or mosses.02324824865320233
0s"Boubovia." 43a : Paraphyses above spirally curved. 02334864875330 Boubovia. 0
0 43b : Paraphyses above straight or slightly curved.02334864885340234
0s"Octospora." 44a : Sp smooth or ornamented, with guttules. Apothecia disc-shaped or cup-shaped, 0.1-1 cm broad ; margin membranous, often dentate or fimbriate. Often together with mosses. 02344884895350 Octospora. 0
0s"Aleuria." 44b : Sp regularly reticulate or with prominent ridges, with two guttules. Apothecia disc-shaped or deeply cup-shaped, 1-12 cm broad. Often on naked soil. 02344884905360 Aleuria. 0
0 45a : Apothecia globose, turbinate, pulvinate or disc-shaped.02354584915370236
0 45b : Apothecia cup-shaped or ear-shaped.02354584925380245
0 46a : On dung.02364914935390237
0 46b : On soil or wood.02364914945400240
0s"Ascodesmis." 47a : Sp broadly ellipsoid, subglobose or globose, with brown ornamentation. Apothecia whitish, pulvinate to globose, very simple, without excipulum cells, 0.08-0.18 mm broad. 02374934955410 Ascodesmis. 0
0 47b : Sp ellipsoid or fusoid, hyaline, smooth.02374934965420238
0 48a : Apothecia turbinate, white, 0.1-0.3 mm broad ; outside furfuraceous. Asci opening by a split down to an annular thickening near the apex, with 8 to 128 fusoid sp. Winter and early spring. 02384964975430 See Ascozonus.0
0 48b : Apothecia globose to pulvinate, white, yellow or brown, with 8 to 2500 sp in asci.02384964985440239
0 49a : Apothecia subglobose and subimmersed or disc-shaped and superficial, yellowish to brownish, 0.1-1 mm broad. Asci cylindric to almost globose, with 8-2500 sp, with operculum or rupturing down to a ring-like thickening below apex ; sp ellipsoid, without de Bary bubbles. 02394984995450 See Thelebolus.0
0s"Coprotus p.p." 49b : Apothecia pulvinate to disc-shaped, superficial, white, greyish, yellow, orange, 0.1-1 mm broad. Asci cylindric to club-shaped, with 8-256 sp, operculate ; sp ellipsoid, with de Bary bubbles. 02394985005460 Coprotus p.p. 0
0 50a : On soil.02404945015470241
0 50b : On wood.02404945025480244
0 51a : Apothecia white or whitish.02415015035490242
0 51b : Apothecia purplish or violet.02415015045500243
0s"Pulvinula p.p." 52a : Sp globose, smooth. Apothecia white, pulvinate to disc-shaped, 0.5-2 mm broad. 02425035055510 Pulvinula p.p. 0
0s"Chalazion." 52b : Sp ellipsoid, thick-walled, with semiglobose warts. Apothecia whitish, pulvinate, 0.3-0.6 mm broad. 02425035065520 Chalazion. 0
0s"Marcelleina." 53a : Sp globose, smooth or with warts or ridges. Apothecia disc-shaped, 3-6 mm broad. 02435045075530 Marcelleina. 0
0s"Smardaea." 53b : Sp ellipsoid to fusoid, coarsely ornamented with rounded warts. Apothecia disc-shaped, 0.5-2 cm broad. 02435045085540 Smardaea. 0
0s"Miladina p.p." 54a : Apothecia pulvinate, 0.5-1 cm broad, yellowish, orange or ochraceous. Sp broadly ellipsoid, verruculose, with many guttules. On wet wood (Pachyella (Pezizaceae) with non-amyloid asci will key out here). 02445025095550 Miladina p.p. 0
0 54b : Apothecia thin, membranous, 0.3-1.2 cm broad, brownish red, paler towards the margin, which is irange, or greenish yellow in young specimens. Sp ellipsoid, smooth, without guttules. 02445025105560 See Karstenella.0
0s"Geopyxis." 55a : On burnt ground. Apothecia regular, substipitate, 0.5-1.2 cm broad, ochraceous to greyish brown, with yellowish white margin. Sp ellipsoid, smooth, without guttules. 02454925115570 Geopyxis. 0
0 55b : On soil.02454925125580246
0s"Otidea p.p." 56a : Apothecia eccentric, split down on one side or ear-shaped, rarely cup-shaped, sessile or stipitate, yellow, ochraceous with pink tinge, or brownish to olivaceous, whitish near the pubescent base of the stem. Sp ellipsoid, with two guttules, smooth ; paraphyses often hooked. 02465125135590 Otidea p.p. 0
0 56b : Apothecia cup-shaped.02465125145600247
0s"Arpinia." 57a : Apothecia stipitate, whitish to cream, 0.5-1.5 cm broad, margin crenate ; outside furfuraceous. Asci bifurcate at the base ; sp broadly ellipsoid, smooth, when mature with one large guttules. 02475145155610 Arpinia. 0
0s"Tarzetta p.p." 57b : Apothecia sessile or stipitate, hymenium yellowish grey, greyish or pale ochraceous, 0.2-4 cm broad, margin crenate ; outside furfuraceous, concolorous with or slightly darker than hymenium. Sp ellipsoid, smooth, with two large guttules. 02475145165620 Tarzetta p.p. 0
0s"Stephensia." 58a : Sp smooth, globose. 02484035175630 Stephensia. 0
0s"Genea." 58b : Sp verrucose, broadly ellipsoid. 02484035185640 Genea. 0
0 Sarcoscyphaceae LE GAL ex ECKBLAD0-21051956600
0s"Pithya." 1a : Apothecia disc-shaped, orange, 0.2-1.2 cm broad, sessile or subsessile. Sp globose. On needles, twigs or branches of coniferous trees. 02493405205680 Pithya. 0
0 1b : Apothecia scarlet or reddish pink. Sp large, ellipsoid. On ± buried twigs or branches of deciduous trees.02493405215690250
0s"Sarcoscypha." 2a : Apothecia deeply cup-shaped, scarlet, 1-4 cm broad, stem 0-2 cm high. Asci maturing individually. 02505215225700 Sarcoscypha. 0
0s"Microstoma." 2b : Apothecia urnulate, reddish pink, 1-1.8 cm broad, stem 2-5 cm long, rooting, sometimes branching. Asci maturing simultaneously. 02505215235710 Microstoma. 0
0 Sarcosomataceae KOBAYASI0-22052457300
0s"Sarcosoma." 1a : Apothecia heavy, globose to broadly cylindric ; hymenium dark brown to black ; excipulum very thick, inside gelatinous. 02513425255750 Sarcosoma. 0
0 1b : Apothecia disc-shaped, cup-shaped or urniform ; excipulum thin, not gelatinous.02513425265760252
0s"Desmazierella." 2a : Hymenium whitish with dark brown dots ; apothecia disc-shaped to turbinate, 1-3 mm broad. On old needles of conifers. 02525265275770 Desmazierella. 0
0 2b : Hymenium dark brownish to black	3.02525265285780253
0s"Urnula." 3a : Apothecia urnulate to infundibuliform, sessile or distinctly stipitate. Sp ellipsoid, hyaline, smooth, without guttules. 02535285295790 Urnula. 0
0 3b : Apothecia cup-shaped or disc-shaped. Sp ellipsoid, ornamented and with guttules, or globose.02535285305800254
0 4a : Hymenium dark brown with violet tinge ; apothecia disc-shaped, 0.3-1 cm broad, outside tomentose, brown. Sp ellipsoid. In associations with the orange Byssonectria terrestris. 02545305315810 See Nannfeldtiella.0
0 4b : Hymenium dark brown. On needles or twigs of coniferous trees, or on Sphagnum tufts.02545305325820255
0s"Plectania." 5a : Apothecia deeply cup-shaped, sessile, 0.5-1.5 cm broad ; hymenium dark brown, outside concolorous, above covered by rust red scales. Sp ellipsoid. 02555325335830 Plectania. 0
0s"Pseudoplectania." 5b : Apothecia cup-shaped to disc-shaped, sessile or stipitate, 0.5-6 cm broad ; hymenium dark brown to black, outside black. Sp globose. 02555325345840 Pseudoplectania. 0
0 Tuberaceae DUMORT.0-23053558600
0s"Choiromyces." 1a : Asci 8-spored. Frb often large, whitish to beige. 02563315365880 Choiromyces. 0
0s"Tuber." 1b : Asci 1-4-(7)-spored. Frb often small or dark coloured. 02563315375890 Tuber. 0
0 Phyllachorales BARR - Phyllachoraceae THEISS. & SYD.0-24053859100
0s"Phyllachora." 1a : Stromata elongate, 2-3 mm long, on living leaves of grasses and herbs, shining black ; perithecia erumpent through the epidermis of the leaf. 0257255395930 Phyllachora. 0
0s"Polystigma." 1b : Stromata forming 2-10 mm broad, yellowish reddish areas on living leaves of trees and herbs ; perithecia developing in the darkened stroma on fallen leaves. 0257255405940 Polystigma. 0
0 Rhytismatales M.E.BARR ex MINTER - Rhytismataceae CHEVALL.0-25054159600
0s"Propolis." 1a : Apothecia immersed in wood of deciduous trees ; hymenium white, pruinose, exposed by rupturing of epidermis or bark. 025895425980 Propolis. 0
0 1b : Apothecia in dark brownish to black stroma on leaves	2.025895435990259
0s"Coccomyces." 2a : Only one apothecium in a dark brown, thin, circular or angular stroma, opening by many fine rays. 02595435446000 Coccomyces. 0
0s"Rhytisma." 2b : Several lineate, wrinkled apothecia in a common, shining, rounded, black stroma. 02595435456010 Rhytisma. 0
0 Xylariales NANNF. - Xylariaceae TUL. & C.TUL. ex WINTER0-26054660300
0 1a : Perithecia immersed in well developed stromata or scanted on cord- or thread-like structures ; the stromata may be greatly reduced in some species.0260265476050261
0 1b :  On dung or perithecia superficial, free, or immersed in plant tissues, with a subiculum or beneath a clypeus or a rudimentary stroma.0260265486060270
0 2a : Stromata stipitate, clavate, strap-like or thread-like, often forked especially at the apices.02615475496070262
0 2b : Stromata sessile, globose, hemispheric, discoid, orbicular, or effused.02615475506080264
0s"Xylaria." 3a : Perithecia not confined to the apex ; stromata with thin brown to black ectostromal crust, flesh remaining white or at least light coloured. 02625495516090 Xylaria. 0
0 3b : Perithecia clustered at the apex of stipitate stromata.02625495526100263
0s"Poronia." 4a : Upper surface of stroma white or pale ; perithecia embedded in a flat disc. 02635525536110 Poronia. 0
0s"Podosordaria." 4b : Stromatal surface brown or black ; perithecia clustered at the apex of stipitate stromata which are rooted in dung or well manured soil. 02635525546120 Podosordaria. 0
0s"Daldinia." 5a : Entostroma with conspicuous concentric zonation ; stromata often almost globose. 02645505556130 Daldinia. 0
0 5b : Entostroma not conspicuously zonate ; stromata of variable size, rarely massive.02645505566140265
0s"Ustulina." 6a : Entostroma white and fleshy when young, collapsing and very brittle when mature. 02655565576150 Ustulina. 0
0 6b : Entostroma pale brown or black when young and at maturity, not collapsing even when old.02655565586160266
0s"Biscogniauxia." 7a : Entostroma pale, composed of both host and fungus tissue, perithecia seated in its base, often with long ostiole necks. 02665585596170 Biscogniauxia. 0
0 7b : Entostroma dark brown or black or red immediately below the surface, composed of fungal tissue only, perithecia inserted in layer just below surface of stromata, ostiole necks short.02665585606180267
0s"Euepixylon." 8a : Sp with a short, distinct, ellipsoid germ slit. 02675605616190 Euepixylon. 0
0 8b : Sp with a short or long longitudinal germ slit.02675605626200268
0s"Entoleuca." 9a : Stromata 0.5-1 cm in diam., in circular or semicircular groups in the host bark, with 1-10(-30) angularly demarcated perithecia in each stroma. 02685625636210 Entoleuca. 0
0 9b : Stromata about 1 mm thick, mostly on wood, effused or in spots.02685625646220269
0s"Nemania." 10a : Ascus-apparatus cylindric hat-shaped (seen in Melzer solution) ; sp with ventral germ slit if present, without loosening epispore. Frb without extractable pigments (put on 10% KOH on piece of frb on white paper) ; anamorph Geniculosporium. 02695645656230 Nemania. 0
0s"Hypoxylon." 10b : Ascus-apparatus broader than high ; sp with dorsal germ slit, often with loosening epispore. Frb with extractable pigments ; anamorph Nodulosporium. 02695645666240 Hypoxylon. 0
0 11a : On dung.02705485676250271
0 11b : Perithecia not in or on dung.02705485686260272
0s"Wawelia." 12a : Stromata prominent, ( covering the dung. Sp without gelatinous coating. 02715675696270 Wawelia. 0
0s"Hypocopra." 12b : Stromata reduced, ( immersed in the dung. Sp with a gelatinous coating. 02715675706280 Hypocopra. 0
0s"Rosellinia." 13a : Perithecia superficial on wood or bark, or on herbaceous stems, often on a subiculum. 02725685716290 Rosellinia. 0
0 13b : Perithecia embedded in plant tissue.02725685726300273
0s"Lopadostoma." 14a : Perithecia in small clusters in bark, with convergent ostiole necks. 02735725736310 Lopadostoma. 0
0s"Anthostomella." 14b : Perithecia solitary or barely coalescing, often beneath a thin clypeus. 02735725746320 Anthostomella. 0
